                </div>
                <div class="kpi-card">
                    <div class="kpi-label">Sharpe-Like Ratio</div>
                    <div class="kpi-value">0.700</div>
                    <div class="kpi-context">Return-to-volatility ratio</div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- MARKET OVERVIEW -->
        <section class="card">
            <h2>1. Market Overview & Long-Term Price Trend</h2>

            <div class="insight-box">
                <h4>Price Trajectory Summary</h4>
                <p>Gold has appreciated from <strong>$273.90</strong> (August 2000) to <strong>$5,377.30</strong> (March 2026),
                representing a <strong>19.7× increase</strong> over approximately 25.5 years. The metal experienced
                distinct bull phases (2001-2012, 2019-2020, 2024-2026) punctuated by corrections, with the most severe drawdown
                of -44.36% occurring during the 2013-2015 period when prices fell from $1,687.9 to $1,050.8.</p>
            </div>

            <h3>Annual Performance Summary</h3>
            <div class="chart-container">
                <canvas id="annualReturnsChart"></canvas>
            </div>

            <h3>Historical Price with Long-Term Trend</h3>
            <div class="chart-container">
                <canvas id="priceTrendChart"></canvas>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- VOLATILITY ANALYSIS -->
        <section class="card">
            <h2>2. Volatility Analysis & Regime Detection</h2>

            <div class="regime-legend">
                <div class="regime-item">
                    <span class="regime-dot low"></span>
                    <span>Low Volatility</span>
                </div>
                <div class="regime-item">
                    <span class="regime-dot medium"></span>
                    <span>Medium Volatility</span>
                </div>
                <div class="regime-item">
                    <span class="regime-dot high"></span>
                    <span>High Volatility</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 1rem 0;">
                Rolling 21-day annualized volatility classified into regimes using 33rd and 66th percentiles as thresholds.
            </p>

            <div class="kpi-grid" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);">
                <div class="kpi-card">
                    <div class="kpi-label">Low-Vol Days</div>
                    <div class="kpi-value" style="color: var(--regime-low);">2,105</div>
                    <div class="kpi-context">Volatility ≤ 12.6% annualized</div>
                </div>
                <div class="kpi-card">
                    <div class="kpi-label">Medium-Vol Days</div>
                    <div class="kpi-value" style="color: var(--regime-med);">2,105</div>
                    <div class="kpi-context">12.6% – 16.9% annualized</div>
                </div>
                <div class="kpi-card">
                    <div class="kpi-label">High-Vol Days</div>
                    <div class="kpi-value" style="color: var(--regime-high);">2,169</div>
                    <div class="kpi-context">Volatility > 16.9% annualized</div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <h3>Rolling Volatility Over Time</h3>
            <div class="chart-container">
                <canvas id="volatilityChart"></canvas>
            </div>

            <h3>Volatility Regime Timeline</h3>
            <div class="chart-container">
                <canvas id="regimeChart"></canvas>
            </div>

            <div class="insight-box">
                <h4>Crisis Period Identification</h4>
                <p>Crisis-level volatility (above 90th percentile) clustered during:
                <strong>2008 Global Financial Crisis</strong> (Lehman Brothers collapse, vol hit ~45%),
                <strong>2011-2012 European Debt Crisis</strong> (gold ETF concerns, vol elevated at ~30%),
                <strong>2020 COVID Shock</strong> (March 2020 crash, vol spike to ~35%),
                <strong>2022 Rate Hike Cycle</strong> (Fed tightening, vol rose to ~25%),
                and <strong>2025-2026 Tariff Wars</strong> (current elevated vol at ~42%).</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- SEASONAL PATTERNS -->
        <section class="card">
            <h2>3. Seasonal & Calendar-Based Patterns</h2>

            <h3>Monthly Returns Analysis</h3>
            <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                Monthly average returns annualized; p-values from t-test (H₀: mean return = 0).
                <span style="color: var(--accent-gold);">Highlighted</span> values are statistically significant (p &lt; 0.05).
            </p>

            <div class="chart-container chart-container-sm">
                <canvas id="monthlyReturnsChart"></canvas>
            </div>

            <h3>Monthly Return Statistics</h3>
            <table class="stat-table">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Month</th>
                        <th>Annualized Return</th>
                        <th>p-value</th>
                        <th>Statistically Significant</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td>January</td>
                        <td class="positive">+1.69%</td>
                        <td>0.0066</td>
                        <td class="significant">Yes (p < 0.01)</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>February</td>
                        <td class="positive">+0.68%</td>
                        <td>0.2819</td>
                        <td>No</td>
                    </tr>
